From a277eb85d761909d05fe0c315689e7ac7e6e0591 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Naveen Sivasamy <naves@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Mar 2026 23:01:16 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] UPSTREAM:PROTOCOL:hostapd: fix incomplete BSS cleanup on
 MBSSID beacon start failure

In hostapd_setup_interface_complete_sync(), when MBSSID is enabled,
hostapd_setup_bss() is called for all BSSs first, followed by a
separate loop calling hostapd_start_beacon() for each BSS. If
hostapd_start_beacon() fails at index j, the error handler only
cleans up BSSs from j down to 0, leaving non-TX BSSs at indices
j+1 through num_bss-1 with wpa_auth allocated but never freed.

These leaked non-TX BSSs have wpa_auth->conf.tx_bss_auth pointing
to the TX BSS's wpa_auth. When the interface is subsequently
disabled and the TX BSS's wpa_auth is freed, tx_bss_auth in the
leaked non-TX BSSs becomes a dangling pointer, causing a
use-after-free when the GTK rekey eloop timer fires and
dereferences it.

Fix by resetting j to num_bss-1 before the cleanup loop so a single
downward pass covers all BSSs initialized by hostapd_setup_bss(),
regardless of where hostapd_start_beacon() failed.

Patch-dependency: none

Signed-off-by: Naveen Sivasamy <naves@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 src/ap/hostapd.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ap/hostapd.c b/src/ap/hostapd.c
index 889c1a0f88..4adaa33a34 100644
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -3848,6 +3848,18 @@ static int hostapd_setup_interface_complete_sync(struct hostapd_iface *iface,
 		for (j = 0; hapd->iconf->mbssid && j < iface->num_bss; j++) {
 			hapd = iface->bss[j];
 			if (hostapd_start_beacon(hapd, true)) {
+				/*
+				 * Start cleanup from num_bss - 1 (not just j)
+				 * so that BSSs above j which were already set
+				 * up by hostapd_setup_bss() but not yet
+				 * reached by hostapd_start_beacon() are also
+				 * cleaned up. Without this, their wpa_auth
+				 * allocations are leaked and tx_bss_auth
+				 * pointers become dangling references into
+				 * freed memory, causing use-after-free crashes
+				 * (e.g. when the GTK rekey eloop timer fires).
+				 */
+				j = iface->num_bss - 1;
 				for (;;) {
 					hapd = iface->bss[j];
 					hostapd_bss_deinit_no_free(hapd);
-- 
